    759  f0bf							; --- VDEL: P0 ON, P1 OFF. NOT the HUD's 13+2 usage — this is the cave's
    760  f0bf							; one-line-ahead discipline, and it is x-INDEPENDENT only when the landing
    761  f0bf							; point of the write is RIGHT of every sprite pixel.
    762  f0bf							; Facts (Stella `Player::grp` / `updatePattern`): without VDEL a GRP write
    763  f0bf							; lands in `myPatternNew` and is rendered immediately, so a mid-line write
    764  f0bf							; affects the CURRENT line when the sprite has not started yet (its pixels
    765  f0bf							; begin at cycle ~(61+X)/3) and the NEXT line otherwise. `myPatternOld`,
    766  f0bf							; the VDEL slot, is latched when the OTHER player is written
    767  f0bf							; (`shufflePatterns`), so VDEL does NOT delay by a line on its own — it
    768  f0bf							; moves the landing point to the other register's store cycle.
    769  f0bf							; Measured store phases (`tools/cycle_ledger.py`, P1 worst path):
    770  f0bf							;   COLUP0 c19 (< all pixels: the per-row colour is always this line),
    771  f0bf							;   GRP0 c35, GRP1 c58, COLUP1 c65.
    772  f0bf							; P0: VDELP0=1 moves its landing from GRP0's c35 (= correct art only for
    773  f0bf							;   X < 44 px) to GRP1's c58 (X < 113 px) and, in the same stroke, aligns
    774  f0bf							;   the art with PlayerColTable (today art row r sits one line above its
    775  f0bf							;   colour for X >= 44). P1 keep VDELP1=0: its latch would be GRP0's c35,
    776  f0bf							;   i.e. a WORSE split than today's c58, and P1's colour would stay at c65.
    777  f0bf							; Every .Line body writes GRP1 exactly once on every path (.Grp1 in-window
    778  f0bf							; or .ObjNoRes blank), so the P0 latch is driven every scanline; that is
    779  f0bf							; the contract `tools/test_vdel_cave.py` guards. HERO clears both bits at
    780  f0bf							; cave entry and uses VDEL only for its HUD text, so this is the one place
    781  f0bf							; we deliberately differ (measured, not guessed).
    782  f0bf		       a9 01		      lda	#1
    783  f0c1		       85 25		      sta	VDELP0
    784  f0c3		       a9 00		      lda	#0
    785  f0c5		       85 26		      sta	VDELP1
    786  f0c7		       85 1f		      sta	ENABL	; HUD-bar leftover off before first visible
    787  f0c9							;   line (.Row row0 BandTab rewrites next)
    788  f0c9
