   2430  f751							; NO REFP1 write here (2026-10-22): REFP1 is ONE register for GRP1, but a
   2431  f751							; frame can draw TWO objects (band pairing, or the 1-of-2 rotation). Driving
   2432  f751							; it from the ACTIVE object made the mirrored miner flip sides every other
   2433  f751							; frame in any room that also had another object. The miner's mirror is
   2434  f751							; gone (a design-based mirror like the LAMP's type 13 needs 32 more art
   2435  f751							; bytes and the table ends 6 B below the $F8C0 pin), so every GRP1 object
   2436  f751							; is drawn unmirrored and REFP1 stays 0 — the bank1 HUD writes 0 for its
   2437  f751							; score, which is exactly what the cave wants.
